/P 44 0 R
/E (Private credit is a growing $1.7 trillion market where companies borrow money from private investment firms instead of traditional banks. After recent banking regulations, traditional banks became stricter about who they lend to. Non-bank lenders like Blackstone stepped in to fill this gap by lending money directly to medium-sized businesses. Companies like this option because they get faster loan approvals and custom payout terms. However, financial experts are worried. These private loans do not trade on public markets, so it is hard to tell how risky or healthy they really are if companies struggle to pay them back. Private credit is now growing fast in places like India, shifting big business loans away from regular banks and into private investment hands.)
/Pg 11 0 R
/K [5]
>>
endobj
