72 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 44 0 R
/E (The BRICS nations are trying to rely less on the US dollar for international business. Instead of launching one single shared currency, they are linking their national payment systems directly. This project, known as BRICS currency connectivity, relies on digital payment platforms like BRICS Pay and mBridge. These platforms allow member countries to connect systems like India's UPI and China's CIPS. As a result, businesses can trade directly in their local currencies like rupees, yuan, or real. This setup bypasses traditional banking networks like SWIFT, which lowers transaction fees and protects these nations from US economic sanctions. The US dollar still dominates global reserves today, but this rising payment system could slowly shrink the dollar's role in world trade over time.)
/Pg 11 0 R
/K [8]
>>
endobj
