75 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 44 0 R
/E (The Bank of India Value Fund is an open-ended equity mutual fund scheme focused on a value investing strategy. Benchmarked against the NIFTY 500 TRI, the fund primarily targets out-of-favor or mispriced stocks. In simple terms, the fund managers look for good companies whose stock prices are currently cheap or underrated by the broader market. By purchasing underappreciated equity assets, the fund aims to deliver capital appreciation over time as market valuations correct upward. When the market eventually realizes their true worth and the stock prices rise, investors make a profit. This approach protects investors from buying overly expensive popular stocks. It is a great option if you have a higher risk tolerance and can stay invested for a few years, because cheap stocks often take time to reach their real value. )
/Pg 11 0 R
/K [11]
>>
endobj
