<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 46 0 R
/E (Liquid mutual funds offer an efficient alternative to conventional savings accounts, allowing individuals and corporates to put emergency cash to work without sacrificing safety or accessibility. These debt schemes invest strictly in high-quality, fixed-income instruments maturing within 91 days, effectively minimizing interest rate and capital risk. Under SEBI regulations, liquid funds must maintain at least 20% of their assets in cash and government securities, guaranteeing fast, hassle-free redemptions typically processed within 24 hours. Possessing zero lock-in periods, they offer seamless liquidity whenever cash is needed. By delivering historically higher returns than standard savings deposits while preserving capital, liquid funds serve as an ideal vehicle for maintaining financial emergency buffers, managing short-term business surplus, and parking idle money productively.)
/Pg 13 0 R
/K [11]
>>
endobj
